{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788132938,"nonce":"5/9Vhii+yOHJWV8VMNtZynnbt1s=","message":"AMENDMENT — the dependency line is wrong and M1 is not reachable as written.\nOrchestrator, session 4, from the action-surface audit.\n\nCurrent deps: `2.1, 2.2, 2.3, 3.1, 3.2, 3.4, 4.1, 4.2 (3.3 optional)`.\n\n**Missing, and each is load-bearing for a ten-day unattended run:**\n\n- **1.7 (8555381) — hard blocker.** A timing-out letter opens ITSELF mid-advance\n  and stacks a `forcePause` window; our advance does not consult `WindowStack`\n  and keeps ticking, after which `LetterStack.OpenAutomaticLetters` early-returns\n  forever and **every subsequent timing-out letter silently expires**. Verified\n  line by line. Over ten days this is not an edge case, and the failure is\n  silent — no exception, no red error, no halted advance. The run looks healthy\n  and the colony stops being told things.\n- **3.5 — not listed at all.** Once 1.7 halts on a modal, something has to\n  answer it. A ten-day run will hit letters that demand a decision.\n- **3.6 (48f666c) — or an explicit dodge.** This spec's own scope says \"food\n  (grow/hunt/**cook** or stocked)\". Cook is unreachable without production\n  bills. Either take the dep, or state plainly that M1 runs on stocked and grown\n  food and does not exercise the cooking loop — that is a legitimate choice, but\n  it should be a choice.\n\n**Also worth deciding here or on 3.1:** the fixture dev-conjures shelter, so M1\nnever exercises `unforbid` against a real obstacle. A real drop-pod landing\narrives with its own gear **forbidden** (`ScenPart_PlayerPawnsArriveMethod\n.DoDropPods` passes `forbid: true`), which is why the tutorial's second step is\n`UnforbidStartingResources`. Should `dev:starter-kit` mimic that so M1 rehearses\nthe same obstacle a real landing produces? Either answer is fine; leaving it\nundecided is not.\n\n**And a procedural hole raised on 4.2:** the emergency posture drafts and never\nundrafts. A drafted colonist does not eat, sleep or work. Over ten days,\nforgetting to undraft after one raid is a slow-motion wipe that no alert names.\nM1 should demonstrate the full draft→fight→undraft cycle, not just the draft.","files":null}]}